M|                                       TEASER                                       
S|       1       EXT. LAKE HOUSE - LATE AFTERNOON                         1           
O|
N,G|               ON OFFRED, moments after we left her in Episode 210, among           
N|               the bare winter trees and stretching shadows.                        
O|
N|               Devastated by her too-brief reunion with Hannah.                     
O|
N|               Frightened for Nick, injured and hauled away by Guardians.           
O|
N|               Reeling from her last, humiliating Ceremony at the hands of          
N|               the Waterfords.                                                      
N|               Offred is alone. Stranded. And very, very pregnant.                  
O|
C,E|                                   OFFRED (V.O.)                                    
U|                         I'm sorry there is so much pain in                         
U|                         this story. I'm sorry it's in                              
U|                         fragments, like a body caught in                           
U|                         crossfire or pulled apart by force.                        
U|                         But there is nothing I can do to                           
U|                         change it.                                                 
P|                            (and then)                                              
U|                         I've tried to put some of the good                         
U|                         things in as well.                                         
N|               The baby kicks, feeling her panic.                                   
O|
C|                                   OFFRED                                           
P|                            (to the baby)                                           
U|                         Shh. It’s okay. It’s going to be                           
U|                         okay.                                                      
O|
N|               Convincing herself as much as the baby. It’s not quite               
N|               working.                                                             
O|
N|               She looks around, trying to get her bearings. Takes a few            
N|               tentative steps to follow the tire tracks.                           
N|               No way. It’s too cold, she’s too conspicuous, she doesn’t            
N|               even know where she is.                                              
O|
N|               What the hell is she going to do?                                    
O|
N|               She notices a GARAGE. Detached from the house.                       
O|
N|               A beat as the significance of this lands on her.                     
O|
N|               Then, moving as quickly as her nine-month belly will let her,        
N|               Offred rushes over.                                                  
O|
O|
O|              THT Production Draft     Ep. 211 "Holly" 1/25/18        2.            
O|
S|       2       EXT. GARAGE - CONTINUOUS                                 2           
N|               Offred tries the side door. Locked.                                  
O|
N|               She rubs frost and dirt off the tiny window with her sleeve.         
O|
N|               Inside, under a cloth cover, is a CAR. Muscular, gas-                
N|               guzzling, pre-Gilead. A beloved hobby project.                       
O|
N|               The possibility of escape. Freedom.                                  
O|
N|               Offred’s panic melts away.                                           
O|
N|               She urgently tries the door again with more force, but               
N|               without success. She needs a key.                                    
N|               Heading back to the house with purpose, she stops dead in her        
N|               tracks.                                                              
O|
N|               A WOLF watches her from the edge of the woods.                       
O|
N|               A wild, dangerous thing, untamed by Gilead.                          
O|
N|               It’s an image from a fairy tale, Red Riding Hood facing off          
N|               against the Wolf, but all too real.                                  
O|
C,E|                                   OFFRED (V.O.)                                    
U|                         My, what big eyes you have.                                
N|               Fear spikes through Offred, but the wolf doesn’t approach.           
O|
C,E|                                   OFFRED (V.O.)                                    
U|                         When I was little, my mom would                            
U|                         never take me to those princess                            
U|                         movies. I remember hating her for                          
U|                         it. But now I know why. In the real                        
U|                         world, you can’t wait for a prince.                        
O|
N|               Wary, she continues on her way back to the house.                    
C,E|                                   OFFRED (V.O.)                                    
U|                         Happily ever after is up to you.                           
O|
N,G|               ON Offred, resolute. She has a chance to get herself and her         
N|               baby out of here, just like she promised.                            
O|
M|                                    END OF TEASER                                   
