M|                                       ACT TWO                                      
S|       7       EXT. GARAGE - LATE AFTERNOON                             7           
O|
N|               Offred ventures back out to the side door. Watchful for the          
N|               wolf, but there’s no sign of it.                                     
O|
N|               She tries the house keys on the keychain until she finds the         
N|               one that lets her in. Things are looking good.                       
O|
S|       8       INT. GARAGE - CONTINUOUS                                 8           
O|
N|               Inside, it’s dim. Offred flips the light switch. Nothing. No         
N|               power out here either.                                               
N|               Glimpses of a little girl’s bicycle along with sand pails and        
N|               water toys hit like punches to the gut, but Offred can’t             
N|               allow her guilt to slow her down.                                    
O|
N|               She pulls the cover off the car, appreciating for a beat how         
N|               cool a ride it is. Mint condition, well cared for.                   
O|
N|               Offred gets in.                                                      
O|
N|               Puts the key in the ignition.                                        
O|
N|               Says a silent prayer and turns the key as she taps the gas           
N|               pedal.                                                               
N|               The RADIO blares on, the LOUD HISS scaring her half out of           
N|               her skin, and the engine RUMBLES to life.                            
O|
N|               She tunes the radio until she hears a FEMALE VOICE, the D.J.         
O|
C,E|                                   D.J. (ON RADIO)                                  
U|                         -- We’ll have another news update                          
U|                         at the top of the hour. This is                            
U|                         Radio Free America, broadcasting                           
U|                         from somewhere in the Great White                          
U|                         North, on your A.M. dial and                               
U|                         online. And now, a tune to remind                          
U|                         everyone who’s listening, American                         
U|                         patriot or Gilead traitor, that we                         
U|                         are still here. Stars and stripes                          
U|                         forever, baby.                                             
M|               [NOTE: Please see the Appendix at the end of the script for          
